# hunter_v2 — Commands

Run from repo root.

## Execution environment

- The project runs inside Ubuntu on WSL2 (Windows host). Any shell command from an agent must be run through `zsh` to pick up the expected `PATH`, `uv`, and Docker CLI wiring — do not assume `sh`/`bash` defaults behave the same.
- Docker Desktop's daemon is exposed to WSL via `/var/run/docker.sock`. If a sandboxed tool call cannot reach the Docker socket (`Cannot connect to the Docker daemon...`), retry the same command requesting full/unsandboxed permissions instead of concluding Docker is down — check with `docker ps` first.
- The local Postgres container (`hunter_v2-postgres-1`) is normally already running via `docker compose up -d postgres`; prefer `docker ps` over re-running `docker compose up` to confirm state before assuming you must start it.
- The local database is regularly refreshed as a full copy of production (see `scripts/sync_local_db_from_prod.py`), so real workshop/account IDs and data volumes are present locally. Treat local data as real production data for safety purposes (no destructive testing against specific real records without care), even though it lives in the local container.

## Environment setup

```bash
uv sync
npm ci
docker compose up -d postgres
uv run python manage.py migrate
uv run python manage.py runserver
```

Optional development seed:

```bash
uv run python manage.py seed_demo_data
```

The project assumes PostgreSQL. SQLite is not part of the normal supported workflow.

## Build and asset commands

```bash
uv run python manage.py tailwind build
uv run python manage.py tailwind build --force
uv run python manage.py collectstatic --noinput
uv run playwright install --with-deps chromium
```

Operational commands:

```bash
uv run python manage.py makemigrations
uv run python manage.py migrate
uv run python manage.py webhook
uv run python manage.py reconcile_webmania_documents
```

## Lint, format, and type-check

```bash
uv run ruff check .
uv run ruff format .
uv run mypy .
```

Tooling facts from `pyproject.toml`:

- Ruff line length: `320`
- Mypy plugin: `mypy_django_plugin.main`
- Django stubs settings module: `config.settings`
- Strict options are enabled, even though several error codes are temporarily disabled during migration

Minimum validation after Python changes:

- run at least one focused test target for the touched behavior
- run `uv run ruff check .`
- run `uv run mypy .` when you changed typed Python code or signatures

## Test commands

```bash
uv run python manage.py test
uv run python manage.py test apps.finance
uv run python manage.py test apps.customer
uv run python manage.py test apps.workorder
uv run python manage.py test apps.finance.test_tax_classes
uv run python manage.py test apps.customer.test_list_filters
uv run python manage.py test apps.stock.test_financial_entries
uv run python manage.py test apps.finance.test_tax_classes.TaxClassServiceTests
uv run python manage.py test apps.customer.test_list_filters.CustomerListViewFilterTests
uv run python manage.py test apps.finance.test_tax_classes.TaxClassServiceTests.test_sync_tax_classes_persists_remote_payload_locally
uv run python manage.py test apps.customer.test_list_filters.CustomerListViewFilterTests.test_customer_list_search_matches_without_accents_and_case
uv run python manage.py test --keepdb
uv run python manage.py test --verbosity 2
```

Important testing reality:

- Many tests live as top-level app files like `apps/finance/test_tax_classes.py` instead of `tests/` packages.
- Do not assume `apps.<app>.tests...` paths exist.
- First inspect the actual filename before choosing the single-test target.
- If a prior run was interrupted or used `--keepdb`, the `test_<DB_NAME>` database may already exist and `manage.py test` will prompt interactively to delete it. In a non-interactive agent shell, add `--noinput` to auto-recreate it instead of hanging on stdin.
